A/B: auto-create a ubiblock for the fit-a / fit-b UBI volumes.

openwrt-one boots from UBI via fitblk, which binds to the block device of the
volume pointed at by /chosen/rootdisk. The kernel only auto-creates a ubiblock
for volumes named exactly "rootfs" or "fit" (491-ubi-auto-create-ubiblock...),
but our A/B layout names the two firmware slots fit-a / fit-b. Without a ubiblock
for fit-a/fit-b, fitblk finds no block device, the root fs never mounts, and the
kernel panics ("VFS: Cannot open root device"). Extend the auto-create match to
fit-a / fit-b so the active slot's volume gets a ubiblock that fitblk can bind.
Both slots get a ubiblock; fitblk uses the one whose of_node matches rootdisk.

--- a/drivers/mtd/ubi/block.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/ubi/block.c
@@ -582,7 +582,9 @@ static void ubiblock_create_auto_rootfs(struct ubi_volume_info *vi)
 	struct ubi_volume_desc *desc;

 	if (strcmp(vi->name, "rootfs") &&
-	    strcmp(vi->name, "fit"))
+	    strcmp(vi->name, "fit") &&
+	    strcmp(vi->name, "fit-a") &&
+	    strcmp(vi->name, "fit-b"))
 		return;

 	desc = ubi_open_volume(vi->ubi_num, vi->vol_id, UBI_READONLY);
